{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VA943krQgNkDKBxy2SjEYS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Kubernetes Secret API Reference - Field Descriptions\n\n## Top-Level Secret Description\n\n\"Secret holds secret data of a certain type. The total bytes of the values in the Data field must be less than MaxSecretSize bytes.\"\n\n## Field Descriptions\n\n### 1. `data`\n\"Data contains the secret data. Each key must consist of alphanumeric characters, '-', '\\_' or '.'. The serialized form of the secret data is a base64 encoded string, representing the arbitrary (possibly non-string) data value here. Described in https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4648#section-4\"\n\n### 2. `stringData`\n\"stringData allows specifying non-binary secret data in string form. It is provided as a write-only input field for convenience. All keys and values are merged into the data field on write, overwriting any existing values. The stringData field is never output when reading from the API.\"\n\n### 3. `immutable`\n\"Immutable, if set to true, ensures that data stored in the Secret cannot be updated (only object metadata can be modified). If not set to true, the field can be modified at any time. Defaulted to nil.\"\n\n### 4. `type`\n\"Used to facilitate programmatic handling of secret data. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/secret/#secret-types\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de781c13-d417-46ad-9a54-21565baee277","uuid":"e6b16f22-8107-4422-b7be-da8d05ded627","timestamp":"2026-08-24T08:33:53.445Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":562610,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Kubernetes Secret API Reference - Field Descriptions\n\n## Top-Level Secret Description\n\n\"Secret holds secret data of a certain type. The total bytes of the values in the Data field must be less than MaxSecretSize bytes.\"\n\n## Field Descriptions\n\n### 1. `data`\n\"Data contains the secret data. Each key must consist of alphanumeric characters, '-', '\\_' or '.'. The serialized form of the secret data is a base64 encoded string, representing the arbitrary (possibly non-string) data value here. Described in https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4648#section-4\"\n\n### 2. `stringData`\n\"stringData allows specifying non-binary secret data in string form. It is provided as a write-only input field for convenience. All keys and values are merged into the data field on write, overwriting any existing values. The stringData field is never output when reading from the API.\"\n\n### 3. `immutable`\n\"Immutable, if set to true, ensures that data stored in the Secret cannot be updated (only object metadata can be modified). If not set to true, the field can be modified at any time. Defaulted to nil.\"\n\n### 4. `type`\n\"Used to facilitate programmatic handling of secret data. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/secret/#secret-types\"","durationMs":5474,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubernetes-api/config-and-storage-resources/secret-v1/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EvbibRgMGQDhfEgbCht1CF","type":"tool_result","content":"# Quotes About Base64 in Secret Data\n\n## Create the Secret\n\n**Quote 1:**\n\"The `data` field is used to store arbitrary data, encoded using base64. The `stringData` field is provided for convenience, and it allows you to provide the same data as unencoded strings.\"\n\n**Quote 2:**\n\"The serialized JSON and YAML values of Secret data are encoded as base64 strings. Newlines are not valid within these strings and must be omitted.\"\n\n## Specify unencoded data when creating a Secret\n\n**Quote 3:**\n\"This field allows you to put a non-base64 encoded string directly into the Secret, and the string will be encoded for you when the Secret is created or updated.\"\n\n**Quote 4:**\n\"When you retrieve the Secret data, the command returns the encoded values, and not the plaintext values you provided in `stringData`.\"\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The page does not contain any explicit statement that \"base64 encoding is not encryption or provides no confidentiality/secrecy.\" Such a security-focused disclaimer is not present in this documentation section."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de781c13-d417-46ad-9a54-21565baee277","uuid":"56fd95d7-6927-4aab-b9ca-5bfba17f470d","timestamp":"2026-08-24T08:33:55.292Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":503565,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Quotes About Base64 in Secret Data\n\n## Create the Secret\n\n**Quote 1:**\n\"The `data` field is used to store arbitrary data, encoded using base64. The `stringData` field is provided for convenience, and it allows you to provide the same data as unencoded strings.\"\n\n**Quote 2:**\n\"The serialized JSON and YAML values of Secret data are encoded as base64 strings. Newlines are not valid within these strings and must be omitted.\"\n\n## Specify unencoded data when creating a Secret\n\n**Quote 3:**\n\"This field allows you to put a non-base64 encoded string directly into the Secret, and the string will be encoded for you when the Secret is created or updated.\"\n\n**Quote 4:**\n\"When you retrieve the Secret data, the command returns the encoded values, and not the plaintext values you provided in `stringData`.\"\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The page does not contain any explicit statement that \"base64 encoding is not encryption or provides no confidentiality/secrecy.\" Such a security-focused disclaimer is not present in this documentation section.","durationMs":4160,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configmap-secret/managing-secret-using-config-file/"}}
