{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMGLRRSBuarhavUxrX9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUGn9rjerjZD8dVtAxysuC","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names/","prompt":"This page is CC BY 4.0 licensed by the Kubernetes Authors, so short attributed quotation is permitted.\n\nQuote exactly (in quotation marks, no paraphrase): the opening paragraph defining Names and UIDs; the sentence about uniqueness of names for a given resource type within a namespace; the definition of a UID and its uniqueness scope; the description of the three name constraint types (DNS Subdomain Names, RFC 1123 Label Names, RFC 1035 Label Names) including their character rules and length limits; and any note about the 253-character limit. Give each with its section heading."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":89068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2044},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de781c13-d417-46ad-9a54-21565baee277","uuid":"5cc4776b-8c44-4e8a-9df0-4d41b9ebfff9","timestamp":"2026-08-24T08:34:11.883Z","request_id":"req_011CeMGLQfnuw5stBfFyA93P"}
